+
+## Flow 5: Late joiner billing backfill
+
+**When**: One-time after deploying late-joiner billing, or when existing students were enrolled mid-term before `billing_cycle_anchor_date` was set.
+
+**Command**: `python manage.py backfill-late-joiner-billing`
+
+**Options**:
+
+- `--schema-name tenant_schema`: Required tenant scope
+- `--course-id 123`: Limit to one course (optional)
+- `--dry-run`: Preview anchors and pending invoices to delete (default when `--apply` omitted)
+- `--apply`: Persist `billing_cycle_anchor_date` and delete pre-anchor `pending_payment` rows
+- `--force`: Recompute anchors even when already set
+
+**Path**: `app_finance/management/commands/backfill-late-joiner-billing.py`
+
+**Logic**:
+
+1. Scan student `UserCourse` rows (tenant-wide unless `--course-id`).
+2. Resolve late-joiner anchor per enrollment (first future session, or join date when no sessions remain on/after join).
+3. Set `billing_cycle_anchor_date` when resolved.
+4. Delete `pending_payment` rows whose `billing_end_date` is before the anchor day.
+
+**Related cleanup-only command**: `delete-pre-join-invoices` (same pre-anchor deletion; optional `--course-id`; does not set anchors).
+
+**Admin workflow**:
+
+1. Run dry-run from internal management commands (Finance) or CLI.
+2. Review affected courses/students and pending invoice ids.
+3. Re-run with `--apply`.
+
+**Not in scope**: Paid or non-pending invoices before the anchor — manual finance review required.
+
